# The committed data files are written by astrosite/src/code/json.ts, using
# JSON.stringify. Prettier cannot be made to agree with it: JSON.stringify always
# puts each array element on its own line, while Prettier collapses a short array
# onto one ("courses": [""]). Letting a formatter near these files would undo the
# writers on every save, which is the exact churn they were changed to stop.
astrosite/src/data/

# The handicap observation log, written by the admin service rather than by a
# build. It lives outside astrosite/ so that committing it does not trip
# deploy-site.yml's path filter, which also takes it out of the rule above.
# Prettier cannot infer a parser for .ndjson and errors on it rather than
# reformatting, so this is the difference between `prettier --check .` passing
# and failing.
data/handicaps/
